KNOWNBUG libstdcxx
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[handler\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Soundness: only an explicit noexcept, noexcept(true) or throw() marks a
function non-throwing (#C_noexcept); a destructor without a
noexcept-specifier is taken as potentially-throwing, so the exception
reaches the handler of main and std::terminate is not called.  The
implicit exception specification of destructors ([except.spec]/7) and of
deallocation functions (/9) has to be computed.
